"In the same way, a mendicant develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors depending on and grounded on ethics, acquiring great and abundant good qualities."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, a mendicant develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors depending on and grounded on ethics, acquiring great and abundant good qualities."@en .

"In the same way, a mendicant develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors depending on and grounded on ethics."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, a mendicant develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors depending on and grounded on ethics."@en .

"In the same way, a mendicant who develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors slants, slopes, and inclines to extinguishment."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, a mendicant who develops and cultivates the seven awakening factors slants, slopes, and inclines to extinguishment."@en .

"In the same way, for a mendicant rational application of mind is the forerunner and harbinger of the arising of the seven awakening factors."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, for a mendicant rational application of mind is the forerunner and harbinger of the arising of the seven awakening factors."@en .

"In the same way, there are these five corruptions of the mind. When the mind is corrupted by these it’s not pliable, workable, or radiant. It’s brittle, and not rightly immersed in samādhi for the ending of defilements."@en owl:sameAs "In the same way, there are these five corruptions of the mind. When the mind is corrupted by these it’s not pliable, workable, or radiant. It’s brittle, and not rightly immersed in samādhi for the ending of defilements."@en .

"It’s when a mendicant develops the awakening factor of mindfulness, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go."@en owl:sameAs "It’s when a mendicant develops the awakening factor of mindfulness, which relies on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripens as letting go."@en .

"It’s when a mendicant meditates by observing an aspect of principles with respect to the five hindrances."@en owl:sameAs "It’s when a mendicant meditates by observing an aspect of principles with respect to the five hindrances."@en .

