"When a mendicant has entered the first absorption, placing the mind, keeping it connected, rapture, bliss, and unification of mind are present."@en owl:sameAs "When a mendicant has entered the first absorption, placing the mind, keeping it connected, rapture, bliss, and unification of mind are present."@en .

"When a mendicant has entered the first absorption, sensual desire, ill will, dullness and drowsiness, restlessness and remorse, and doubt are given up."@en owl:sameAs "When a mendicant has entered the first absorption, sensual desire, ill will, dullness and drowsiness, restlessness and remorse, and doubt are given up."@en .

"When the mind is restless, it’s the right time to develop the awakening factors of tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en owl:sameAs "When the mind is restless, it’s the right time to develop the awakening factors of tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en .

"When the mind is restless, it’s the wrong time to develop the awakening factors of investigation of principles, energy, and rapture."@en owl:sameAs "When the mind is restless, it’s the wrong time to develop the awakening factors of investigation of principles, energy, and rapture."@en .

"When the mind is sluggish, it’s the right time to develop the awakening factors of investigation of principles, energy, and rapture."@en owl:sameAs "When the mind is sluggish, it’s the right time to develop the awakening factors of investigation of principles, energy, and rapture."@en .

"When the mind is sluggish, it’s the wrong time to develop the awakening factors of tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en owl:sameAs "When the mind is sluggish, it’s the wrong time to develop the awakening factors of tranquility, immersion, and equanimity."@en .

"When these seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated they are noble and emancipating, and bring one who practices them to the complete ending of suffering.”"@en owl:sameAs "When these seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated they are noble and emancipating, and bring one who practices them to the complete ending of suffering.”"@en .

"When these seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated they lead to growth and progress.”"@en owl:sameAs "When these seven awakening factors are developed and cultivated they lead to growth and progress.”"@en .

